  "notable_quotes": [
    "Zn2(Atz)2(ox) shows strong low-pressure CO2 uptake with a zero-loading heat of adsorption of 40.8 ± 0.8 kJ mol−1.",
    "Large low-pressure CO2 uptake is attributed to the combination of suitable pore size, pore-lined amine groups, and cooperative CO2 binding.",
    "The adsorption enthalpy does not simply fall with loading; after an initial decrease, DHads rises again and stays above 35 kJ mol−1, indicating cooperative binding."
  ],
